{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790187678,"nonce":"fymhyM7eBL3PrFQyX6F9IE7mb3o=","title":"Generate the GPU plugin's typed resource wrappers and plugin! export table from one gpu.api.rs declaration while retaining the gpu namespace. WebIDL supplies selected enum strings and integer flag namespaces; backend operations remain explicit instead of pretending IDL interfaces describe native ownership or execution.","message":"Implemented locally: caribou-bindgen builds wrappers using normal Caribou classes, Text, Buffer and Enum carriers. The GPU backend is adapted from hlwgpu, with no HashLink primitive table, UTF-16 helper or HL allocator. Shader/label text borrows UTF-8 views; uploads borrow shared buffers and readback writes directly to them after bounds checks. Bind groups use a typed GpuBindings resource rather than packed raw-handle bytes. Native adapter/device requests resolve tickets before constructing their returned resource objects.\n\nThe object API covers compute, buffers and asynchronous mapping, textures/samplers, render pipeline builders, render commands and surfaces. This is the declared backend subset, not complete browser WebGPU; native forwarding for wasm and complete format/descriptor coverage remain outside this implementation. Builds do not depend on the sibling hlwgpu repository.\n\nValidation: generator parsing/diagnostic tests, generated catalog and native resource identity tests, existing handle/request tests, and the rebuilt Haxe fixture. The fixture executes a compute shader on Apple M1 Pro/Metal, reads four transformed integers through shared buffers, verifies oversized upload/readback rejection, and passes with ASH_GC_STRESS=1 WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1. Surface/render presentation and other platforms have not been exercised.\n\nExisting frontend limits still apply: Wren cannot construct arbitrary Caribou enum arguments (80d0ccf1037e66b651d5250897daf19a668c716da73ec0f747272a54b90a02a2), and Zyntax's shared object/buffer/enum transfer remains c5751252b0e8b1e9a019fb93e9db98caf8bc2a9dc5bee7b2f890bfac10344c23.","files":null}]}